ked black  sectioned  and submitted as follows  The small specimen is bisected and entirely submitted in I and J  The larger specimen is serially sectioned and sequentially submitted in K M  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE X 3 5cm fibrofatty tissue with a long suture to denote lateral and a short suture to denote superior  The entire specimen is inked black  and the inferior is overinked in red  Serial sections from lateral to medial are made to reveal a REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE X 1 0cm  tan white  stellate  firm lesion which appears to grossly abut the inferior lateral margin and is approximately 0 2cm from the posterior margin  The parenchyma is predominantly tan white  dense  fibrous tissue with a small amount of admixed tan yellow fat  There is a REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE X 0 5cm  ill defined  tan white  firm area  0 2cm from the inferior medial aspect  Representative sections are submitted as follows  N  tumor to inferior margin  O  tumor to posterior margin  P Q  representative sections of tumor  R  section of ill defined nodule  Gross Description by  KRISTEN SMITH Resident  VIKRAM DESHPANDE  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  Robert Nathan Blatman  M D  REMOVED_MONTH Leslie Shifren  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL MARGINS    EXCISION PART C  BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISION , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 01 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 15 12 CLINICAL DATA  Known left breast cancer by core                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA   SEE TABLE  1   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  WITH MICROCALCIFICATIONS  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  BREAST  LEFT FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  SINGLE FOCUS OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU    REMOVED_DATE CM  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN REMOVED_DATE LYMPH NODES  NO CYTOKERATIN POSITIVE TUMOR CELLS ARE SEEN  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE X 0 3cm  Grade  1  Lymphatic vessel invasion  Not identified  Blood vessel invasion  Not identified  Margin of invasive carcinoma  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  Location of ductal carcinoma in situ  Within and beyond the region of the mass  Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  Focally positive at the medial anterior and medial posterior margins of the specimen  Ductal carcinoma in situ extends to less than 0 2cm from the mid posterior  Section D  E  margin of the specimen along a broad front  Stains for receptors  Requested  Diagnosis by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 16 28                                                                                     BREAST CANCER IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block E   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 16 21 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left axillary sentinel lymph node   are 2 pieces of fibroadipose tissue and lymph node measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  The larger portion of tissue is bisected and is submitted entirely as frozen section  1  the smaller of the two lymph node is bisected and submitted entirely as frozen section  2  Frozen section  1 is now resubmitted as A  and  2 as B  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast lumpectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE fragment of breast tissue with a short stitch demarcating the superior margin and a long stitch demarcating the lateral margin  The anterior surface is inked blue and the posterior surface is inked black  Specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm hemorrhagic biopsy cavity  which lies 0 5cm from the closest  mid posterior  margin  There are surrounding tan white fibrous tissue around the biopsy cavity along with an ill defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm irregular shaped tan white gritty region  which is approximately 1 6cm from the closest  mid posterior  margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is unremarkable  SECTION CODE  C E  biopsy cavity and adjacent mid posterior margin  entirely submitted  F  adjacent nodule and adjacent closest margin  G  medial edge of smaller nodule  H  lateral extent of breast specimen  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  final margin   are multiple fragments of fibro  fatty tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm in aggregate  The entirety of the tissue is submitted as cassettes I N  Resident  AARON CAPLAN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION  1  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION  2  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  PAUL MICHAELS  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL   PART B  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART C  BREAST  LEFT FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISIONAL BIOP , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  21 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  21 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 40 CLINICAL DATA  Stitch at deepest portion along the bottom of the specimen                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST   RIGHT  AND  RIGHT INFERIOR PIECE    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  PREDOMINANTLY LOBULAR BUT ALSO WITH DUCTAL DIFFERENTIATION AND WITH EXTENSIVE INVOLVEMENT OF BIOPSY MARGINS  BOTH SPECIMENS   THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  LOBULAR CARCINOMA  IN SITU  EXTENSIVE  FOCAL FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  Diagnosis by  Robert B  Colvin  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 16 18 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 33     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  Right   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 14 40 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  in two parts  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and designated as follows  Labeled  right breast needle localization specimen   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with an attached needle localization wire and a stitch designating the deep aspect  A specimen X ray accompanies the specimen  The deep aspect of the specimen is inked yellow and sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm irregular  firm  white tan stellate mass extending to the inked lateral and deep margins  A representative section is submitted as FX 1 and the block is saved frozen   Note  no orientation is provided for anatomic medial and lateral orientation of the specimen   The breast tissue away from the main tumor mass shows nodular  yellow white  firm to rubbery fibrous appearing tissue that is also present along the lateral and deep margin  Representative sections from the region of the tumor mass are submitted in cassettes A through C  Representative sections extending across the base of the specimen in the regions of the nodular white rubbery areas are submitted in cassettes D through G  Labeled  inferior piece right breast  outside of tumor   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  It is inked and sectioned to reveal an irregular  firm  white tan stellate portion of the parenchyma  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  This lesion extends to inked margin  A representative section is submitted as FX 2 and the block is saved frozen  Representative sections are submitted for permanent sections in cassettes H through J  Resident  C  Diana Jordan  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST  MAIN SPECIMEN   INFILTRATING AND IN SITU CARCINOMA  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2   RIGHT BREAST  INFERIOR PIECE   INFILTRATING AND IN SITU CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  OZDEMIRLI METIN  NO ADDRESS  O R  Diagnosis by  Asif Rashid  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  Carolyn Diana Jordan  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST PART B  RIGHT BREAST INFERIOR PIECE   report_end  , Unchecked.
