Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  06 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 17 02 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  4 CM  INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  SEE NOTE  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA  LEVEL 1   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 2 OF 9 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  LYMPH NODES   RIGHT AXILLARY  LEVEL 2    TUMOR EMBOLI IN PERINODAL LYMPHATICS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN TWO OF TWO LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  LYMPH NODES   RIGHT AXILLA  HOT SPOT  1  CT  90    EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN ONE OF ONE LYMPH NODE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor penetrates the capsule of one lymph node  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 50                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In t