h are submitted in toto as cassette A  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   are 20 cores of tan yellow fibrofatty tissue ranging in size from 0 4cm to 2 0cm which are submitted in toto as cassettes B D  Gross Description by  TARA HARRIS Resident  PAULA ARNELL  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  Eren D Yeh  M D  Nassar M Beydoun  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT 6 O CLOCK   CORE BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 09 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  EXTENDING TO INKED MARGIN  NOTE  Tumor extensively involves most of the tissue submitted  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is seen  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 47                                                                                     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   RIGHT  BIOPSY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   3   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 463 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 5  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 56     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 28 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm mass of fibroadipose tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a homogeneous tan  finely granular surface  Representative sections frozen as frozen section  1  The frozen block is sent to Cox 5 for estrogen and progesterone receptor analysis  Sections sent for BRDU  Remainder is submitted in cassettes A and B  Resident  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST TISSUE   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 11 01 CLINICAL DATA  Positive fine needle aspiration biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm tumor focally extends to the resection margin  It invades into adjacent skeletal muscle and approaches to within less than 1mm of the deep margin  Small foci of ductal carcinoma in situ  comprising less than 1  of the total mass  are present within the invasive component  and a single small focus is seen in parenchyma away from the invasive component  There is no evidence of lymphatic invasion  Diagnosis by  Teri L  Moore  MD Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 16 49                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 08 05 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a 5 x 3 x 1 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with an attached REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm skin ellipse at one edge and a 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm piece of skeletal muscle at the opposite deep edge  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm firm  irregular white tan  relatively well defined mass extending to the inked deep resection margin  The mass is 2 5cm from the skin ellipse  No frozen section done  Submitted in cassettes A through K  Resident  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST  LUMPECTOMY   VERY SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  BUT TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  Metin Ozdemirli  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
