Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 14 31 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  reduced breast tissue  is a 566 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm aggregate of fibrofatty tissue with attached tan skin  Sectioning reveals 50  dense white fibrous tissue and 50  tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue  No gross abnormalities identified  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes A J  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast tissue  is a  REMOVED_CASE_ID  gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm breast with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of axilla  The specimen is surfaced by an REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm tan unremarkable skin with a centrally located REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm grossly unremarkable areolar nipple complex  Sectioning reveals 40  dense white rubbery fibrous tissue and approximately 60  tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue  The most dense rubbery tissue is contained in the upper and lower outer quadrants  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm  and comes to 1 0cm from the deep margin  1 0cm from the superior margin  5cm from the lateral margin  1 5cm from interior margin  and 4 5cm from the medial margin  There are no distinct tumor masses or previous biopsy cavities identified  There are 11 tan pink nodules dissected from the axillary tail consistent with lymph nodes  the largest being REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  K  Fibrosis toward lateral deep margin in the outer quadrant L  Fibrosis to superior margin M  Fibrosis to deep margin in outer quadrant N  Fibrosis in the upper outer quadrant O  Fibrosis in the outer quadrant P  Fibrosis towards inferior