Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  06 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 16 43 CLINICAL DATA  Moderately differentiated ductal carcinoma of left breast which was diagnosed REMOVED_DATE                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED GRADE REMOVED_DATE  20   AND EXTENSIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  80   CRIBRIFORM TYPE   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The ductal carcinoma in situ surrounds the biopsy cavity extending in an irregular rim which is 2 5cm in maximum dimension and is present within a fraction of a millimeter of multiple superior inked margin  located medial to the original biopsy site  Medially the in situ component blends imperceptibly with an area of infiltrating carcinoma 1 2cm in maximum dimension in histologic section  2 of 14 lymph nodes contain metastatic carcinoma  No definitive vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  2  LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA  MICROSCOPIC FOCUS  3  BIOPSY CAVITY WITH HEMORRHAGE  FAT NECROSIS AND GIANT CELL TYPE REACTION  Diagnosis by  Leonard Atkins  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 10                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen which includes a REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm skin ellipse with an eccentrically located REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm areola located within 0 6cm of the medial margin and central REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm nipple  The epidermal surface is unremarkable  The undersurface of the specimen is smooth and glistening  however  on sectioning there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm smooth walled biopsy cavity filled with maroon clot  This cavity is situated within 0 1cm of the closest inked margin which is the deep margin  Surrounding the cavity is an area of fat necrosis and interparenchymal hemorrhage  Sectioning through the remaining portion of the specimen reveals fibroadipose tissue which is traversed by thick  pale tan  fibrous bands  The specimen also includes an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm axillary tail  A node dissection is undertaken and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm aggregate of tan brown lymph nodes is submitted in A E  Section Code A E   lymph nodes F   closest margin  deep G   additional representative deep section H J   representative sections of the superior surface K   representative lateral section L M   representative medial sections N   areola O P   additional sections adjacent to the superior portion of the biopsy cavity Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT  , Unchecked.
