as personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast lumpectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm portion of tan red fibrofatty tissue with two localization wires in place  A short black stitch designates the superior margin  and a long black stitch designates the lateral margin  The posterior margin is inked black  the anterior margin is inked blue  the superior margin is inked green  and the inferior margin is inked yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm hemorrhagic cavity consistent with previous biopsy site which come to 0 7cm of the anterior  1 0cm of the posterior  1 2cm of the inferior  1 4cm of the superior  0 8cm of the medial  and   2 0cm of the lateral margins  A silver metal clip is noted within the cavity  Surrounding the cavity is dense gray white fibrous tissue with yellow orange discoloration consistent with fat necrosis  Also noted is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm from gray tan nodule which comes to 0 7cm of the posterior  0 7cm of the inferior  1 3cm of the anterior  1 5cm of the superior  0 9cm of the medial  and   2 0cm of the lateral margins  No other gross abnormalities are identified  Representative sections are submitted from lateral to medial as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the lateral margin radially sectioned as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   the medial margin en face as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   the cavity with clip as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and the nodule adjacent to the cavity as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remainder of the specimen is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received are four containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   Tonna  REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  final margin superior   are two irregular portions of tan pink fibrofatty tissue with no orientation measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  Sectioning reveals no apparent lesions or other gross abnormalities  and the specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  final margin inferior   are two irregular portions of tan pink fibrofatty tissue with no orientation measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  Sectioning reveals no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  and the specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  final margin medial   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm aggregate of tan pink fibrofatty tissue with no orientation  Sectioning reveals no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  and the specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  final margin lateral   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm aggregate of tan pink fibrofatty tissue with no orientation  Sectioning reveals no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  and the specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1  QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  The invasive and in situ tumor cells show a similar hormone receptor and HER 2 protein expression profile  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  The t