ed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 17 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  and unit number  are two parts  Labeled  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm lumpectomy specimen with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm skin ellipse  Centrally  the skin contains a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm area of induration  with accentuated dermal markings  No scars are noted  Directly underlying the skin changes  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm firm  stellate and lobular  tan yellow mass  extending to within 2 0cm of the deep resection margin  and 1 5cm of the closest lateral resection surface  The parenchyma fibrous septae extends from the mass and abut the inked surfaces  the remaining breast parenchyma is unremarkable  Section Code  A B  skin with underlying mass  C  lateral margin  D  deep margin  E  mass  F G H  septae extending to inked surfaces  Labeled  Axillary contents  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm aggregate of fatty tissue  dissected to reveal approximately 13 lymph nodes  REMOVED_DATE to 2 0cm in maximum diameter  soft to rubbery  All nodes submitted in I J K  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Kenneth Kenji Tanabe  M D  PART A  RIGHT AXILLARY CONTENTS PART B  RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
