Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D  Resident  Omer Yilmaz  M D   Ph D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D  CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 63 year old woman with a history of LCIS  DCIS and FEA in the right breast  She underwent an excision on REMOVED_DATE  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  A  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  FOCAL LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH MILD DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  USUAL TYPE  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS  3  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  An immunohistochemical stain for e cadherin performed on slides  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is negative in areas of lobular carcinoma in situ and supports the diagnosis  B  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  APPROXIMATELY REMOVED_DATE CM  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH MILD DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  USUAL TYPE  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS  SEE TABLE 1  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU TUMOR SIZE  REMOVED_DATE CM GRADE  1 CALCIFICATIONS  Limited to benign changes  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  The distance to all margins measures 0 2cm or greater  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  See prior report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  C  SKIN  RIGHT BREAST   EXCISION  SKIN AND SUBCUTIS WITH NO SIGNIFICANT PATHOLOGIC ABNORMALITY  D  SKIN  LEFT BREAST   EXCISION  1  SKIN AND SUBCUTIS WITH SCAR  2  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 4 containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  right   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm right breast simple mastectomy specimen which is partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm wrinkled white nipple and areolar complex with a centrally located 1 5cm in diameter grossly unremarkable nipple  The specimen is oriented with a stitch designating 12 o clock  The specimen is inked as follows  Posterior   black  anterior   blue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm hemorrhagic biopsy cavity within the lower outer quadrant which extends to within 3cm of the posterior margin and 1 2cm of the anterior margin  The cavity is surrounded by gray white fibrous tissue and areas of fat necrosis  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm  slightly indurated gray white area within the upper inner quadrant which measures 9cm from the biopsy cavity  The second area extends to within 2 4cm of the posterior margin and 3 0cm of the anterior margin  The remainder of the cut surface consists of lobulated tan yellow fat with interspersed areas of nodular  dense gray white fibrous tissue  The lateral aspect of the specimen is palpated  no lymph nodes are identified  Also received within the container is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm irregular portion of lobulated tan yellow fibroadipose tissue which is unoriented  The second portion of tissue is entirely inked black and sectioned to reveal a lobulated tan yellow fatty cut surface with no masses or lesions grossly identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the lower outer quadrant biopsy cavity surrounding fibrous tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of tissue between the cavity and the second indurated area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the indurated area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue away from the biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the separately received portion of tissue  Received fresh  labeled  left   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 7cm left 