Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 54 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast carcinoma with lumpectomy 7 years ago                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor is very poorly circumscribed and is REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm in cross section  as measured from the slides  It focally extends to within less than 1mm of the resection margin in several foci  A circumscribed nodule of tumor associated with a small rim of lymphocytes is also present  It is not possible to determine if this is a separate tumor nodule  or a small lymph node completely replaced by carcinoma  Extensive lymphatic permeation is present  There is no evidence of an in situ component  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Teri L  Moore  MD Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 49                                                                                     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   RIGHT BIOPSY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   3   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 463 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 5  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 02     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 38 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue with localizing wire in place and accompanying x ray  Specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a firm  white  well defined 0 6cm nodule  adjacent to a firm  white  0 6cm poorly defined extending to within 0 1cm of the inked margin  A representative section from the area close to the margin is frozen as FX  1 and saved frozen  A thin sliver sent for BRDU  Lesion submitted in A F  Additional tissue submitted as G and H  Resident  James Kirby  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Lisa H  Lerner  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Asif Rashid  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
