stics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 16 15 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  additional axillary tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm portion of adipose tissue which contains three  tan red  focally hemorrhagic  rubbery lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  The specimen is entirely submitted as follows  A  two whole lymph nodes B  largest lymph node  bisected C  remainder of specimen Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm breast with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm attached axilla  The overlying REMOVED_DATE x 8 5cm tan skin has a eccentric REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm inverted nipple  Specimen sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm irregular  rubbery  hemorrhagic area that is located 3 0cm inferior and 1 5cm lateral from the nipple and extends to within 2 5cm from the inferior skin margin and 0 5cm to the deep margin  This 2 6cm area is grossly consistent with a previous biopsy site  Adjacent to the biopsy site  along the medial aspect  are tan white foci suspicious for calcifications  this REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm area is located 0 5cm superior and deep to the biopsy site  Located 3 5cm lateral to the inferior site is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan white diffusely hemorrhagic area consistent with a second biopsy cavity  This area extends to within 1 5cm of the deep margin and is contiguous with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 1