OSIS  1   1A   1B   SENTINEL NODE LEFT AXILLA 750    There is no evidence of carcinoma in two lymph nodes  0 2   Await sentinel node  workup         CLINICAL HISTORY  Carcinoma in situ of breast  Ductal carcinoma in situ with positive margins   now undergoing left mastectomy     SPECIMENS SUBMITTED   A  SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION  LEFT AXILLA  750  B  BREAST MASTECTOMY  LEFT  C  ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR MARGIN  LEFT BREAST  D  SKIN EXCISION  LEFT MASTECTOMY FLAP    GROSS DESCRIPTION  A  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME    REMOVE_MRN     sentinel node left axilla 750   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm piece  of fibroadipose tissue to include a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm node which is bisected  and frozen entirely as FX 1 and FX 1A  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   respectively and a REMOVED_DATE  x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm node which is entirely frozen as FX 1B  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remaining  fibroadipose tissue is submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    JS     Received are 2 containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN   CP     B  Received fresh  labeled  left mastectomy  short stitch superior  long stitch  lateral   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 1cm mastectomy specimen with a short suture  designating superior and a long suture designating lateral  The overlying REMOVED_DATE x  2 0cm irregular  tan portion of skin appears unremarkable and exhibits an  unremarkable portion of nipple areolar complex  The anterior margin of the  specimen is inked blue and the posterior is inked black  The posterior margin  is remarkable for a REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm defect which exposes an underlying hemorrhagic  cavity  The edges of the defect are inked yellow  The specimen contains a REMOVED_DATE  x REMOVED_DATE x 3 3cm hemorrhagic cavity in the outer central breast which is  contiguous with the previously described defect and comes to within 0 8cm of  the anterior ma