oned  and entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  medial lateral margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan yellow to pink lobulated portion of fibrofatty tissue  There is a suture along one aspect designating the new margin  The new sutured margin is inked black  the specimen is serially sectioned  and entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm tan yellow lobulated portion of lymph node bearing fatty tissue  Multiple lymph nodes are identified ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 1cm in maximum dimension  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four whole possible lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four whole possible lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two whole possible lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected lymph node  Gross Dictation by Jennifer Nash  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Kristina Braaten M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Kristina Braaten M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erbB 2 Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Elena F Bracht