Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  08 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  08 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 10 CLINICAL DATA  History of breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  RESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  ONE MICROSCOPIC FOCUS  REMOVED_DATE CM  CONFINED TO THE BIOPSY SITE  SLIDE I   PRESENT REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE NEAREST INKED MARGIN   SEE NOTE   NOTE  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  Multiple levels examined  This tumor is histologically similar to the tumor in the previous biopsy   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    LYMPH NODES  AXILLARY   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN TWELVE OF TWELVE LYMPH NODES   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Immunoperoxidase stains for epithelial and lymphoid markers were performed  the results confirm the abscence of metastatic carcinoma   MEDIAL MARGIN   BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED   LATERAL MARGIN   BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED   SUPERIOR MARGIN   BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED   INFERIOR MARGIN   BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 17 26 Staff Pathologist  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are four containers  Labeled  Medial  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm tan soft tissue fragment  entirely frozen as Frozen Section  1  and now submitted in cassette A  Labeled  Lateral margin  is a tan soft tissue fragment  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm  entirely frozen as Frozen Section  2  and now submitted in cassette B  Labeled  Superior margin  is a tan red soft tissue fragment  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm  entirely frozen as Frozen Section  3  and now submitted in cassette C  Labeled  Inferior margin  is a tan red soft tissue fragment  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm  entirely frozen as Frozen Section  4  and now submitted in cassette D  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two parts  Labeled  Re excision left breast biopsy site  previous diagnosis cancer  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fibrofatty tissue fragment  with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm overlying skin ellipse with a central 1 5cm healed scar  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm ill defined biopsy site extending to one margin  consisting of tan rubbery tissue and surrounding bright yellow tissue  No firm areas are palpated  No cavity is identified  The tan tissue extends up to within 0 1cm of the overlying skin ellipse  No other lesions are identified  Section Code  E  biopsy site at closest margin  representative section  with overlying skin ellipse  F I  biopsy site  representative sections  J  unremarkable breast parenchyma  Labeled  Axillary nodes  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm fibrofatty tissue framgent sectioned to reveal 12 rubbery tan pink lymph nodes ranging in size from 0 4cm in greatest dimension to 1 5cm  All have a tan pink cut surface  One half of each node is submitted in cassettes K through M  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT  MEDIAL   FAT NECROSIS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  BREAST  LEFT  LATERAL   FAT NECROSIS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  3  BREAST  LEFT  SUPERIOR MARGIN   NORMAL  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  4  BREAST  LEFT  INFERIOR   FIBROSIS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART A  MEDIAL PART B  LATERAL MARGIN PART C  SUPERIOR MARGIN PART D  INFERIOR MARGIN PART E  AXILLARY NODE PART F  BREAST  LEFT   REEXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
