97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 09 14 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm portion of breast  inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 3cm irregular  firm and gritty nodule in the center of the specimen  approximately 0 3cm from the posterior margin  The specimen is submitted entirely in Cassettes A G  with the nodule in Cassettes A C  the superior margin Cassette D  and the inferior margin in Cassette E  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm portion of breast  with unremarkable yellow fatty cut surface  No discrete lesion is grossly identified  The specimen is submitted entirely in Cassette H L  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT  NO GROSS LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  GROSS SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  BREAST  LEFT  A REMOVED_DATE CM NODULE HIGHLY SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  HENRY DONG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
