Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  28 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  28 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 12 42 CLINICAL DATA  A 58 year old woman with suspicious calcifications within the left breast and a biopsy showed carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY    RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU ABOUT BIOPSY SITE  SOLID  CRIBRIFORM  AND MICROPAPILLARY TYPES   SEE NOTE     FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH FIBROSIS  MICROCYSTS AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA    FIBROADENOMA  0 5 CM     FAT NECROSIS  FIBROSIS  FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION  CONSISTENT WITH BIOPSY SITE    SKIN WITH SCAR    THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN TWENTY FIVE OF TWENTY FIVE LYMPH NODES  0 25   NOTE  The resection margins are free of tumor  No invasive component is seen  LYMPH NODE  BIOPSY    THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  ONE LYMPH NODE  Diagnosis by  Kathleen K  Hansen  MD Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 31                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled  left modified mastectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 8cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with an axillary tail  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 8cm  There is a curved healed skin incision line  measuring 5 0cm in the superior medial quadrant  The overlying skin ellipse measures REMOVED_DATE x 11 5cm and the nipple is everted and measures 4 0cm from the inferior margin and 11 0cm from the lateral margin  The previously described incision line is 2 0cm from the superior margin and 1 2cm from the medial skin margin  The skin is grossly unremarkable  On sectioning through the breast  there is a large REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 5cm blood filled cavity  Its wall is red brown with adherent green tan and fibrinous exudates  The tissue 