Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 18 50 CLINICAL DATA  47 year old with history of right breast carcinoma in  REMOVED_CASE_ID   Tx ed with lumpectomy  axillary node dissection  XRT and and chemotherapy  Now has recurrent right breast cancer and is going to have right breast MRM and left breast simple mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  100   MULTIPLE SCATTERED FOCI BOTH ADJACENT TO AND AWAY FROM THE BIOPSY CAVITY  THE LARGEST FOCUS SPANNING AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM AS MEASURED ON A GLASS SLIDE AND EXTENDING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  2  BIOPSY CAVITY WITH FIBROSIS  CHRONIC INFLAMMATION  GIANT CELL REACTION AND HEMORRHAGE  NOTE  No definitive vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified    BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH FIBROSIS  CYST FORMATION  APOCRINE METAPLASIA MICROCALCIFICATIONS Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 18 30                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 59     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  RESULTS PENDING The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 16 22 GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen is submitted in two parts each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  Received fresh in a container  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a mastectomy specimen  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm  On the specimen is an ellipse of skin  measuring REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm with a nipple and areola measuring 2 0cm in greatest dimension  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a biopsy cavity immediately adjacent to the ellipse of skin  The cavity measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm and a stitch is present to indicate the previous biopsy site  This area is serially sectioned to reveal a smooth biopsy cavity inner wall with focal areas of yellowish white discoloration in the wall of the cavity  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 0 4cm in greatest dimension  These areas extend to within 0 1cm of an inked resection margin  The remainder of the parenchyma is composed mainly of adipose tissue with focal areas of ill defined white  firm tissue  The nipple and overlying skin is grossly unremarkable  no axillary tail accompanies the specimen  SECTION CODE  A E  representative sections of the cavity  from the region of the stitch with deep resection margin F J  representative sections of nodular areas from the upper outer quadrant  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a simple mastectomy specimen  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm which includes an ellipse of skin  measuring REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  with a nipple  Grossly the skin and nipple appear unremarkable  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal multiple areas of ill defined  firm  whitish  tan nodules  The largest measuring 4 0cm in greatest dimension and extends to within 0 3cm of the deepest resection margin  In focal areas there are multiple cysts in the nodular areas  SECTION CODE K T  representative sections of the nodular areas U  representative section of the nipple  Resident  KWAN KEITH  NO ADDRESS                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  PART B  BREAST  LEFT    report_end  , Unchecked.
