ly from the indurated area is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm healed linear scar which comes to 0 9cm of the lower inner skin margin  The resection margin is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm firm stellate gray white tumor mass with focal hemorrhage and bright yellow orange areas  contiguous with the indurated skin lesion and arising in the mid portion of the specimen  The mass comes to 3 2cm of the deep  0 9cm of the inferior superficial and 1 2cm of the superior superficial margin  Centrally the mass shows a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm hemorrhagic cavity consistent with previous biopsy site  Between the mass and the deep margin are multiple firm tan white nodules ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm  The former comes to 1 0cm from the deep margin and the remaining nodules are  2 0cm from the deep margin  The remaining tissue is composed of 40  dense gray white fibrous tissue and 60  tan yellow adipose tissue  The fibrous tissue is focally gritty  Sectioning of the possible axillary tail reveals no apparent lymph nodes  Representative sections are submitted as follows  B C  Deep margin closest to tumor and satellite nodules D  Firm tan white nodules between tumor and deep margin E  Tumor to inferior superficial margin F  Tumor to superior superficial margin G H  Tumor with hemorrhagic biopsy cavity I  Tumor J K  Focally gritty fibrous tissue away from tumor Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast skin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm strip of unremarkable tan pink skin  The margin is inked black  the specimen is serially sectioned and representative sections are submitted as L  Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  SHABIN NANJI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  SENTINEL LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resid