 was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  03 MAY 01 at 14 51 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm fibroadipose tissue fragment with a localization needle  There is a long stitch designating the lateral and a short stitch designating the superior margins  The specimen is inked as follows  deep black  anterior blue  lateral orange  medial red  The specimen is sectioned from superior to inferior serially to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 1 5x 1 0cm hemorrhagic biopsy cavity surrounded by a tan firm stellate mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  The biopsy cavity is 1 5cm from the deep and the anterior margins  1 4cm from the lateral margin  1 0cm from the superior margin  1 0cm from the inferior margin and 2 0cm from the medial margin  The stellate mass surrounding the biopsy cavity is 0 2cm from the anterior margin   0 1cm from the deep resection margin  1 0cm from medial margin and 1 2cm from lateral margin  Representative sections of the biopsy cavity and surrounding stellate mass are submitted as follows  Section code  A  superior margin  en face  B  inferior margin  en face  C  anterior margin D E  deep and medial margins F G  lateral margin H  additional sections of biopsy cavity  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right sentinel lymph node  hot and blue 434  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan nodule which is bisected and entirely submitted in cassette I  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right axillary node contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fibroadipose tissue fragment  Sectioning of the specimen reveals multiple lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm in greatest dimension  The large lymph nodes are bisected and half of each are submitted in cassettes J K  The smaller lymph nodes are entirely submitted in cassettes L M  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  final shaved margin of breast  are multiple fibroadipose tissue fragments aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  Specimen is sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes N R  Resident  QUN DONG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  David Bent Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL   EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY CONTENTS   EXCISION PART D  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISIONAL BI , Unchecked.
