Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  15 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  15 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 09 52 CLINICAL DATA  Seventy seven year old female with an excisional biopsy of right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  FOCALLY LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM OF AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  NOTE  Perineural invasion is present  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 32 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 09 46     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  and unit number  and  right breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm yellow pink fibroadipose tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a stellate white  firm mass with a gritty cut surface abutting the inked margin  The mass is entirely submitted in A D  Representative sections of grossly negative tissue are submitted in cassette E  Resident  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  LESION TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  H  Thomas Aretz  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
