Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  05 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  05 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 12 CLINICAL DATA  History of intraductal carcinoma with positive margins on a previous right breast excision                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  1  FOCAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  2  FOCAL ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA  INVOLVING DUCTS  3  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  4  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  WITH FAT NECROSIS  FIBROSIS  HEMOSIDERIN DEPOSITION  AND FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION  5  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL COMEDOCARCINOMA  NOTE  The separate piece of breast tissue in the same container also shows no evidence of carcinoma  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 22 Consulting Pathologist s   Dennis Sgroi  M D                                                                                  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name  unit number  and  right breast tissue  is an 82 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm breast re excision specimen with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm skin ellipse containing a 3 8cm long  centrally located  longitudinal  well healed scar  A long suture designates the inferior surface and a short suture designating the superior surface of the skin ellipse  The specimen is entirely inked in black  then double inked red on the superior surface  yellow on the inferior surface  and blue on the lateral surface  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm cystic cavity that is filled with dark brown liquid  located subjacent to the skin ellipse  3 5cm from the deep resection margin  1 4cm from the inferior resection margin  1 0cm from the superior resection margin  0 9cm from the lateral resection margin  and 0 3cm from the medial resection margin  The biopsy cavity is surrounded by an irregular  firm  focally yellow colored tissue and an ill defined  firm  white to tan tissue that extends to the superior  lateral  inferior  and focally to the deep soft tissue resection margins  The remaining breast parenchyma is composed of soft  lobulated adipose tissue  Section code  A  skin with scar and biopsy cavity  with closest lateral and medial soft tissue resection margin B  biopsy cavity and medial resection margin C  biopsy cavity and lateral resection margin D  biopsy cavity with superior resection margin E  inferior resection margin F  deep resection margin  firm  white area  G H  biopsy cavity with lateral resection margin  representative sections  including firm white area I  firm white area  representative sections  inferior margin J  firm white area  representative section  lateral margin Also in the specimen container  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an ill defined  white  firm breast tissue that approaches the inked margins  and is interposed with yellow  lobulated adipose tissue  Representative sections are submitted in K through N  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   RE EXCISION OF RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
