Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 24 CLINICAL DATA  Status post needle localization                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  90    GRADE 2 OF 3  REMOVED_DATE CM IN LARGEST DIMENSION  SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  10    COMEDO TYPE  NOTE  Both components  infiltrating and in situ  extend to within 1mm of the inked resection margin  Neither blood vascular nor lymphatic invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 26                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with thi