ch clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 11 24 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  MRM    REMOVED_CASE_ID  grams   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 5cm mastectomy specimen  with a skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 17 0cm  The areola is REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm  and the nipple is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  Attached is an axillary tail  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm  On the skin surface are three scars  the first is a 4 0cm linear scar  which is inferior and medial  and is 1 9cm from the nipple  the second scar is a 3 0cm linear scar  which is inferior and lateral  and 9 5cm from the nipple  In addition  there is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm oval scar  which is medial and inferior to the nipple  and is 8 5cm from the nipple  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior   blue  posterior   black  Sectioning reveals a well defined  firm  white gray mass that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm  and is 2 0cm from the deep margin  Representative sections of the mass and its nearest margin are submitted in cassettes A D and R T  Also noted is a brown gray  firm  stellate appearing lesion  that is 1 6cm from the skin surface  This lesion measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The lesion contains one REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm cyst that contains old hemorrhage  Representative sections of the cyst like lesion are submitted in cassettes E F  The remaining breast parenchyma consists of yellow  soft adipose tissue with intermixed white fibrous tissue and is grossly unremarkable  Representative sections of breast parenchyma away from the lesion  are submitted in cassettes G H and U AA  Axillary lymph nodes are identified  the largest of which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  The smaller lymph nodes are submitted en