 ellipse  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  The specimen is serially sectioned along the medial to lateral axis to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm biopsy cavity in the upper inner quadrant that measures 5cm to the anterior margin and 2cm to the posterior margin  The biopsy cavity has a tan pink to hemorrhagic cut surface  Located 0 3cm lateral to this cavity is 3 x 2 x 1 1cm cavity that contains brown serous fluid that is located 2 5cm to the anterior margin and 1 3cm to the posterior margin  The remaining breast parenchyma is fatty with scant to moderate amounts of tan white rubbery fibrous tissue  No additional mass or lesion is noted  The clip is not identified  The upper outer quadrant tissue is palpated for lymph nodes and no lymph nodes are grossly appreciated  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of posterior margin to smaller hemorrhagic cavity radially   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire hemorrhagic cavity submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of area between hemorrhagic cavity and cystic lesion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of cyst wall to posterior margin at closest point   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire cystic lesion that is medial to the hemorrhagic cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative tissue away from lesion  INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1   RIGHT SENTINEL LYMPH NODE   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  Lymph Node  Right Axilla   Sentinel    Excision PART B  Lymph Node  Right Axilla   Sentinel   2   Excision PART C  Breast  Right   Simple Mastectomy PART D  Breast  Left   Simple Mastectomy PART E  Cryostat Frozen Section  slide only   report_end  , Unchecked.
