n block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm tan yellow soft tissue aggregate  The fat is removed and two potential lymph nodes are identified measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  inked black   and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  The larger node is bivalved  Both lymph nodes are frozen as FX 1 and submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   right breast   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 6cm right mastectomy specimen including an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm extension of fibrofatty tissue consistent with axillary tail  A black stitch designates the 12 o clock position  The specimen is partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 3 4cm tan pink skin ellipse with a central unremarkable REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm nipple  The skin shows a 2 5cm healed linear scar along the upper outer aspect which comes to 0 3cm of the margin  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm defect along the anterior aspect  arising 0 7cm superior lateral to the skin  The defect communicates with a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm cavity  consistent with previous biopsy site  The cavity is lined by hemorrhagic gray white fibrous tissue  and comes to 2 0cm of the posterior margin  Along the anterior inferior aspect of the cavity is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm indurated tan pink mass  which is 1 3cm of the cavity  0 2cm of the anterior margin and 1 8cm of the posterior margin  The remaining breast tissue is focally dense gray white fibrous tissue with no discrete lesions or other gross abnormality  Section of the axillary region re