ing the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erbB 2 Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows    Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells    Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells    Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   30  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 24   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 11 37 45AM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Lymph Node  Left Axilla   Sentinel    Excision PART B  Breast  Left   Excision PART C  Breast  Left  Final Margin Anterior   Excision PART D  Breast  Left  Final Margin Lateral   Excision PART E  Breast  Left  Final Margin Superior   Excision PART F  Breast  Left  Final Margin Medial   Excision  report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  20 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  20 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 11 CLINICAL DATA  Locally advanced right breast carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  REMOVED_DATE CM EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of the tumor  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   RESECTION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN TWO OF SEVEN LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor does not transgress the lymph node capsules  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 01                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 11 32 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  long stitch axillary contents  short stitch superior   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm mastectomy specimen with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm skin ellipse  which contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm nipple  A firm  white tan REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm area of discoloration surrounds the nipple  An attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm axillary tail is also present  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm firm  white mass with yellow speckles and grossly extends to 1 5cm from the deep resection margin  Further sectioning of axillary tail reveals several lymph nodes  several of which are firm  white tan while others are soft pink  The lymph nodes range in size from REMOVED_DATE 2cm in greatest diameter  SECTION CODE  A C  Representative section of mass with closest deep resection margin  D F  Additional representative sections of mass  G   Representative section of mass with overlying nipple  H I  Representative sections of unremarkable breast parenchyma away from mass  J L  Axillary lymph nodes  Also received in the same container is a separate piece of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm soft  yellow piece of fat  which is sectioned to reveal unremarkable parenchyma  Representative sections are submitted in Cassette M  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Un