er quadrant  which extends to 0 7cm from the anterior margin and 3 3cm from the posterior margin and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm poorly delineated nodular fibrous area in the central lower to mid breast  which extends to 2 0cm from the posterior margin and is 3 5cm from the first described nodule  The lower outer quadrant contains several gritty firm tan foci as large as REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  which extend to 0 3cm from the posterior margin  The lateral tissue contains one small lymph node  The following sections are submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lower inner quadrant nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multinodular fibrous area in central lower to mid breast   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lower outer quadrant including firm tan foci   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sections  Unfixed  labeled  Leslie S  Stein  REMOVED_DATE  left breast   is an 18 x 16 x 4 0cm left mastectomy specimen partially surfaced by a 15 x 5 6cm ellipse of skin with an unremarkable areola and nipple  A suture designates the superolateral aspect  The anterior margin is inked blue  and the posterior black  The specimen contains four nodules  The first occupies the  11 o clock  position  spans REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm  and extends to 0 2cm from the posterior margin and 0 4cm from the anterior margin  It consists of indurated  triangular  gray white and centrally hemorrhagic tissue  The second sits 4 0cm inferomedial to the first  occupies the  8 o clock  position  spans REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x o 7cm  and extends to 0 4cm from the posterior margin  The mass appears well defined  feels indurated  and consists of tan white and focally hemorrhagic tissue  The third mass occupies the  7 o clock  position at a distance of 0 9cm from the second mass and 6 3cm from the third mass  spans REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  and